1
00:05:57,692 --> 00:06:03,692
What we do in life echoes in eternity.

2
00:11:55,384 --> 00:12:01,384
Gladiator is a action, drama, adventure film directed by Ridley Scott.

3
00:17:53,076 --> 00:17:59,076
After the death of Emperor Marcus Aurelius, his devious son takes power and demotes
Maximus, one of Rome's most capable generals who Marcus preferred.

4
00:23:50,769 --> 00:23:56,769
Eventually, Maximus is forced to become a gladiator and battle to the death
against other men for the amusement of paying audiences.

5
00:29:48,461 --> 00:29:54,461
Maximus, played by Russell Crowe.

6
00:35:46,153 --> 00:35:52,153
Commodus, played by Joaquin Phoenix.

7
00:41:43,846 --> 00:41:49,846
Lucilla, played by Connie Nielsen.

8
00:47:41,538 --> 00:47:47,538
Proximo, played by Oliver Reed.

9
00:53:39,230 --> 00:53:45,230
Marcus Aurelius, played by Richard Harris.

10
00:59:36,923 --> 00:59:42,923
Gracchus, played by Derek Jacobi.

11
01:05:34,615 --> 01:05:40,615
Gladiator is a 2000 epic action adventure drama film directed by Ridley Scott and written by
David Franzoni, John Logan, and William Nicholson from a story by Franzoni.

12
01:11:32,307 --> 01:11:38,307
It stars Russell Crowe, Joaquin Phoenix, Connie Nielsen, Oliver
Reed, Derek Jacobi, Djimon Hounsou, and Richard Harris.

13
01:17:30,000 --> 01:17:36,000
Crowe portrays Maximus Decimus Meridius, a Roman general who is betrayed when Commodus, the
ambitious son of Emperor Marcus Aurelius, murders his father and seizes the throne.

14
01:23:27,692 --> 01:23:33,692
Reduced to a slave, Maximus becomes a gladiator and rises through the ranks of the
arena, determined to avenge the murders of his family and the emperor.

15
01:29:25,384 --> 01:29:31,384
The screenplay, initially written by Franzoni,
was inspired by the 1958 Daniel P.

16
01:35:23,076 --> 01:35:29,076
Mannix novel Those About to Die.

17
01:41:20,769 --> 01:41:26,769
The script was acquired by DreamWorks Pictures, and
Scott signed on to direct the film.

18
01:47:18,461 --> 01:47:24,461
Principal photography began in January 1999 and wrapped in May of that year.

19
01:53:16,153 --> 01:53:22,153
Production was complicated by the script being rewritten multiple times and
by the death of Oliver Reed before production was finished.

20
01:59:13,846 --> 01:59:19,846
Gladiator had its world premiere in Los Angeles, California, on May 1, 2000.

21
02:05:11,538 --> 02:05:17,538
The film was released in the United States on May 5, 2000, by DreamWorks
and internationally on May 12, 2000, by Universal Pictures.

22
02:11:09,230 --> 02:11:15,230
The film grossed $466 million worldwide, becoming the second-highest-grossing film of 2000,
and won five Academy Awards, including Best Picture and Best Actor for Crowe.

23
02:17:06,923 --> 02:17:12,923
A sequel, Gladiator II, was released in 2024.

24
02:23:04,615 --> 02:23:10,615
The film explores themes of gladiator, rome, italy, arena, senate, roman empire.

25
02:29:02,307 --> 02:29:08,307
The tone is emotional.
